Time-Keeper-Recurrence

Rules that say when something happens again: RFC 5545 recurrence rules, cron
expressions in Punk::Queue's grammar, and named arguments such as
every(2, 'weeks', on => [qw(tue thu)]), walked in any time zone and in any
calendar Time::Keeper has (RFC 7529). A rule with dates added and removed,
or several rules, is a set; sets are read and written as iCalendar text;
rules and sets are stored as text with their zone by name, and a rule says
itself in English words (describe). A C ABI lets a
scheduler written in C compile a rule and walk it, or ask for a cron's next
occurrence in one call.

INSTALLATION

Time::Keeper::Zone and Time::Keeper must be installed first: this builds
against their headers.

    perl Makefile.PL
    make
    make test
    make install

